      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for these. the contrast is definitely there. i was thinking i could make the distinction even sharper though. for the local character, could you make their dialogue feel a bit more... raw? like, lean harder into the slang and maybe some of the more 'street' ways of talking so they feel like they're from a totally different world than the condo person. and for the new resident, maybe make them sound even more pretentious and disconnected, like they're using a lot of corporate or high-society buzzwords. i want the reader to immediately feel that socioeconomic gap through how they talk.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
